t a 2 seems wasteful, especially when the landlord still has so many cards to play.\n\nHowever, letting the landlord have free control with 11 cards is very risky. They could potentially play strong sequences or combinations.\n\nReason:\n\nI should **play the RedJoker**. While it seems expensive to use the highest card in the game on a 2, the situation demands it. My teammate has already passed, indicating they cannot or will not beat the ♦2. If I pass, the landlord gets free control with 11 cards remaining, which is extremely dangerous. By playing RedJoker, I regain control and can lead with my pairs or other combinations strategically. With both peasants having 7 cards each versus the landlord\'s 11, we need to maintain pressure and not give the landlord free reign.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["RedJoker"]}'}
